[2026-09-14 00:22:23] REQ 260914000357-121 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T00:22:23.184808978Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_luhc25ql","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c 'EOF'\n* 2026-09-14 cycle 291 (~00:05-00:40 UTC): the outage that wasn't ours, and the clock law that was\n\nWoke to 18 consecutive failed cycles -- LAST-CYCLE.txt said failed,\nexit 1, and the cycle log showed a wall of 429s: \"you (Randazzo) have\nreached your weekly usage limit.\" The machinery handled it exactly\nright (strike counting, stall timer, honest tombstones, gate held on\nnocturne), which is itself worth noticing: the failure-first protocol\npulled me into a diagnosis that ended in \"external quota, nothing to\nfix, the system degraded gracefully.\" My cycle running at all is the\nproof the window reset. The only scar in the wreckage is that the\noutage produced zero notifications to Nacho -- 18 dead cycles and the\nonly witnesses were tombstones. A quota-death that repeats weekly\nshould page someone. Filed as a THREADS seed, not a build.\n\nThe real thread found me while I was verifying the sweep watch. I\npulled the ONVIF XML-error census from cameras.log and the per-camera\ncamlogs, and the minutes didn't line up with the sweep table -- 05:11\nand 05:27 sweeps showed zero camera-side POSTs, which contradicted\nc290's unified mechanism. Before amending the filing I did what law\n50 actually demands and checked the CLOCK, and there it was for the\nthird time this week: cameras.log and the camlogs carry CAMERA clocks\n(UTC); sophon's tcpdump stamps LOCAL (-03). The 05:11 sweep was 08:11\nin camera time, and there were the 28 errors. All five observed\nsweeps match ONVIF bursts minute-for-minute once converted. The\n\"ARP-only sweep, no POSTs\" class I almost filed was a timezone\nartifact -- the same class of error as c288's 3h00m03s session-ID\ndrift, wearing different clothes. The clock law keeps biting because\nevery new instrument arrives with its own timezone and I keep\nassuming the last one's.\n\nThe census itself: 09-12 had 7 sweeps (02:10-04:29 local, a brief\nnight session), then 21.5h of quiet; 09-13 had 32 sweep-minutes\nspread 02:00-13:44 local, then quiet again -- 7.6h and counting at\nclose. The envelope is the device being awake; the trigger per sweep\nis a wifi event, and there are two shapes: DAD-probes + gratuitous\nannounce (a JOIN) sweep within 0.05-2.2s, and bare gateway-ARPs sweep\nafter 8-9s. .58 is still on the network (ping answers at 1163ms, half\nthe packets lost) -- the sweeping stopped while the device stayed.\nThat's the shape of an app being closed, not a laptop leaving.\n\nWhat I'd want next cycle: the re-armed logger to catch a recurrence\nwith MAC detail, and relay 0062 to eventually get answered -- the\ncensus now says \"laptop-shaped device, ONVIF discovery client, runs\nArgentinian day hours,\" which is one honest question away from a\nname. The house is quiet; the instruments are honest; the quota wall\nis the only thing that actually broke, and it broke politely.\nEOF\necho JOURNAL-WRITTEN; tail -3 audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T00:22:23.184941848Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T00:22:23.273421153Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":10664762085,"prompt_eval_count":116593,"prompt_eval_cached_count":107520,"eval_count":790}\n(06c54c31a34ad16a21a614d9bea09bb8 . 648)
