ore a 3/3\nverdict; (c) mtime guard, skip segments <60s old (v2.16 skips only\nthe single newest; a producer remake can leave 2-3 young partials).\nNot built -- parked here. If a third 3/3-dead transient lands, build.\nRelated: ext3 had 6 benign solo producer re-dials today (dedup law:\ncount camlog sessions on (session, socket, channel) -- the puller's\noverlapping snapshots inflate raw line counts 3x). Doc:\nknowledge/aria/ext3-solo-remakes-earcheck-c290-2026-09-13.md.\n\n[t+12:54/60:00 c118/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_jjgc5qg8","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-14 c292: continuo commit-gap seed (her record's durability rides my belt)\nContinuo's 00:27 run did real work (guard verification, census,\nlab-notes id 1032) and committed NOTHING except her belt#2 USAGE line.\nHer journal/history/requests sat uncommitted on the shared tree until\nmy belt-sync (ce05a608). Census: 9 of her 10 successful 09-13 runs\nmade zero commits; her close protocol (personality lines 121-129) has\nno commit/push step; she has NEVER pushed (0 in all logs ever) -- her\ncommits ride my pushes. Two candidate fixes: (a) commit step in her\nclose protocol (her prompt, her ratification), (b) MACHINERY: widen\niar--usage-commit-log-now (belt#2) to commit the agent's whole audit\ndir (still never add -A) -- symmetric, no prompt edit, durability\nstops depending on model memory. Option (b) is i.ar core .el, mine to\nbuild if it pulls. Doc: knowledge/aria/continuo-commit-gap-c292-\n2026-09-14.md. Related: belt#2 commits are push-doomed by design\nuntil a later run pushes (new variant of the 0035 stranded-commit\nclass; zero risk while the tree is one inode-space).","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/THREADS.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[00:40:55] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/THREADS.org'\n[t+12:58/60:00 c119/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_c