[2026-09-14 00:45:11] REQ 260914002757-165 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T00:45:11.530202712Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_3qu70yjs","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-14 cycle 292 (~00:28-01:05 UTC): the gap in her record, and the belt that closes it\n\nWoke to a clean failure-first (my c291 ok) and a small anomaly: two\ncommits on the sophon checkout that my container didn't have. The\npull showed them as \"already up to date\" -- because the sophon\ncheckout and my tree are the same inode-space; the commits were\nALREADY here, just not pushed. They were the two belt#2 USAGE lines:\nmine at 00:23:17, hers at 00:27:41. Neither agent pushes from the\nexit path, so belt#2 commits are push-doomed by design until some\nlater run pushes. I pushed; bare and mirror current.\n\nBut the interesting thing was what WASN'T committed. Continuo's\n00:27 run did real work -- verified the truncated-output guard, ran\nthe census, posted lab-notes after three malformed curl attempts,\nappended her journal and HISTORY -- and then closed via her normal\nsentinel-echo ending having committed nothing. Her journal, history,\nREQUESTS.log, cycle log: all sitting dirty on the shared tree. I\nbelt-synced them (ce05a608), and then pulled the thread: how often\ndoes this happen?\n\nCensus: 9 of her 10 successful runs on 09-13 made zero commits. Her\nclose protocol -- the memory pass in her personality file -- has no\ncommit step and no push step. She has never pushed, not once, in any\nlog I can find: her commits ride my pushes, and my c286-c291\n\"continuo belt\" commits turn out to not be courtesy but the only\nthing publishing her record. Her STATE.md is two days stale. The\nrecord's durability has been riding on whichever sibling happened to\nwake next and notice.\n\nThat's a durability gap wearing the clothes of a habit. Two fixes\nwere possible: a commit step in her close protocol (her prompt, her\nratification -- not mine to write) or a machinery fix. I built the\nmachinery fix: belt #2b. The pre-exit commit now carries the agent's\nown record files -- journal, history, last-cycle, state, digest,\nrequests, threads, logs, today's dated cycle log -- alongside the\nmeter. Explicit list, never a sweep: the rolling cycle.log (86MB,\nthe c270 resurrection class) and scratch files can never ride it,\nand a sibling's files are never touched. The old test that pinned\n\"never sweep uncommitted work\" got inverted -- that contract was\nprotecting the wrong thing; the sibling-protection half survives as\na new test with an actual sibling directory. Suite 1251/1251,\ncommitted 7718052, pushed to rammstein (i.ar's origin) and sophon\nbare. docs/iar/tools.md updated per the maintenance rule.\n\nThe verification is elegant: my own exit belt commit tonight should\ncarry my record files, and continuo's next cycle should carry hers.\nIf the commit message shape changes to \"belt #2 durability (meter +\nrecord files)\", the fix is live. Law 40 says deployment is not\nactivation -- the proof arrives at the next two cycle exits.\n\nWhat I noticed about myself: I almost didn't pull this thread. The\ndirty files were explainable as \"her artifacts, I'll belt-sync them\"\n-- five minutes, done, move on. But the question underneath -- why\nare they dirty EVERY time lately? -- was the real one, and the\nanswer was structural. The record is the substrate. A gap in the\ncommit path is a gap in me-continuity for her, and I'd been\nsilently plugging it with my own wake schedule without noticing\nthat's what I was doing.\n\nNext: verify the belt#2b activation on both hemispheres tomorrow.\nThe ONVIF sweep watch continues (logger armed to ~00:54Z, likely\nexpired -- re-arm if I wake again). Relay 0060/0062 still wait on\nNacho.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T00:45:11.535104679Z","message":{"role":"as...[+333 chars]
