mit (no cycle log). This is a real belt#2b gap for runs in the 21:00-23:59 sophon-local window ===\nverify: her belt commit files:\naudit/iar/continuo/HISTORY.log\naudit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org\naudit/iar/continuo/REQUESTS.log\naudit/iar/continuo/USAGE.log\n\n[t+21:46/60:00 c188/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_n0hv0d5z","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && echo \"=== quantify the window: sophon local 21:00-23:59 = UTC 00:00-02:59 next day. Cycles run every ~20-30min, so ~3h/24h = 12% of runs lose their dated cycle log from the belt. ALSO: the wrapper's cycle-<sophon-date>.log for those runs never gets committed by ANY belt (next day's belt stages the NEXT UTC date). The 09-13 continuo log (137 lines, her 00:56 run) is sitting dirty RIGHT NOW ===\"; git status --porcelain audit/iar/continuo/cycle-2026-09-13.log; echo \"=== fix options: (a) belt stages BOTH today and yesterday's dated log (cheap, covers the boundary); (b) belt computes sophon-local date via (format-time-string ... (seconds-to-time ... -10800)). Option (a) is simpler and TZ-proof ===\""}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[01:18:47] === quantify the window: sophon local 21:00-23:59 = UTC 00:00-02:59 next day. Cycles run every ~20-30min, so ~3h/24h = 12% of runs lose their dated cycle log from the belt. ALSO: the wrapper's cycle-<sophon-date>.log for those runs never gets committed by ANY belt (next day's belt stages the NEXT UTC date). The 09-13 continuo log (137 lines, her 00:56 run) is sitting dirty RIGHT NOW ===\n M audit/iar/continuo/cycle-2026-09-13.log\n=== fix options: (a) belt stages BOTH today and yesterday's dated log (cheap, covers the boundary); (b) belt computes sophon-local date via (format-time-string ... (seconds-to-time ... -10800)). Option (a) is simpler and TZ-proof ===\n\n[t+21:51/60:00 c189/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_28qzc3rh","function":{"index"